Vendored into FlowGuard as the demo application that the CI pipeline builds, tests, scans and
deploys. Kept unmodified: cmd/, pkg/, ui/, go.mod, go.sum, Dockerfile, Dockerfile.xx, Makefile,
LICENSE, README.md, .gitignore. Not vendored: the upstream CI workflows, Helm charts, deploy/,
kustomize/, timoni/, otel/, test/ and release-signing files.
Changes made in FlowGuard, if any, are listed below with their date and reason.

Changes:
2026-10-25  Security fixes (FlowGuard decision D24). Go toolchain 1.23 -> 1.26.10 (go.mod
            toolchain, Dockerfile, Dockerfile.xx; Go 1.25 is end-of-life and cannot take the
            fixes). Modules: google.golang.org/grpc 1.67.1 -> 1.83.2, golang.org/x/net 0.30.0
            -> 0.60.0, golang.org/x/text replace floor 0.19.0 -> 0.42.0, go.opentelemetry.io/otel
            and otel/sdk 1.30.0 -> 1.44.0, github.com/golang-jwt/jwt/v4 4.5.0 -> 4.5.2,
            github.com/klauspost/compress 1.17.9 -> 1.18.7, and the versions they require.
            'as' -> 'AS' in both Dockerfiles. No source code changed then.
2026-10-26  Runtime image alpine:3.20 (end-of-life 2026-04-01) -> alpine:3.24 in both Dockerfiles.
2026-10-26  SOURCE MODIFIED (FlowGuard decision D19, amended): fault injection for graded bad
            versions. New pkg/api/http/fault.go and fault_test.go; four flags in
            cmd/podinfo/main.go (--fault-error-rate, --fault-latency-ms, --fault-jitter-ms,
            --fault-fraction, also PODINFO_FAULT_* env), four Config fields and the middleware
            registration in pkg/api/http/server.go. Off by default; user routes only; probes and
            the metrics port are never touched.
2026-10-27  SOURCE MODIFIED (D19, amended again): fault settings can change at run time.
            fault.go keeps them in an atomic pointer, adds a memory leak at a fixed rate and an
            admin handler (GET/PUT/DELETE /fault) served on the metrics port only with
            --fault-admin (PODINFO_FAULT_ADMIN); server.go builds the middleware before the
            metrics server and registers it when --fault-admin is set; main.go adds the flag.
            Injected errors answer {"error": "internal error", "hostname": ...}.
2026-10-28  Dockerfile and Dockerfile.xx: git installed in the build stage, so the go command can
            fetch modules the proxy cannot serve (runtime image unchanged).
2026-10-27  SOURCE MODIFIED (FlowGuard decision D29): pkg/api/http/env.go drops variables starting
            with PODINFO_FAULT_ (a release's settings, from its release Secret) from GET /env;
            env_test.go checks it. Every other variable is still listed.
